Working Well Together: Apprentice Session Plan

Oct 7, 2026

Session overview

A 105-minute, in-person session that helps new apprentices understand psychological safety, name how they like to communicate and work, and agree how they'll make room for each other's preferences. It ends with a draft team working agreement they own.

Audience: New software apprentices, ideally 6 to 16 people (works best in groups of four).

Duration: 1 hour 45 minutes, including a 10-minute break. It runs straight after the paper plane factory, which goes first after lunch.

By the end, apprentices will be able to:
– Explain psychological safety in their own words and why it matters for engineering teams
– Describe their own communication and working preferences, and recognise that others differ
– Suggest practical ways to accommodate preferences that aren't their own
– Contribute to a team working agreement they'll revisit during their first few months

Materials: Sticky notes (two colours), marker pens, flipchart or whiteboard, printed personal user manual handout (one each), timer visible to the room, and a slide or flipchart with the 1-2-4-All prompts.

Room set-up: Tables of four, with space for pairs to turn to each other. If remote, use breakout rooms of two and four, plus a shared Miro or Mural board.

